# Reference letter scans.
#
# These are other people's personal data, not mine: letterhead carries direct
# phone numbers, private addresses and signatures, and once an image is pushed
# to a public repo it is in the history for good. So they are ignored by
# default and have to be added deliberately, with a force-add, after the
# referee's contact details have actually been covered over:
#
#   git add -f public/letters/tsanakas.jpg
#
# See public/letters/README.md.
public/letters/*.jpg
public/letters/*.jpeg
public/letters/*.png
public/letters/*.webp
public/letters/*.pdf

# Wrangler's local state, and the Worker's local secrets. .dev.vars.example
# is the committed template; .dev.vars is the copy with real values in it.
.wrangler
.dev.vars
